# Plan: customer satisfaction rating

Spec: `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` (approved, Mai Do, 2026-01-12). Written 2026-10-07 without the user present; every question below was answered with its recommendation and the plan is built on those answers ("assumed, not confirmed"). Nothing is built yet.

Test command: `node --test` (README; `npm` is not installed on this host, so run it directly). Baseline before any phase: run it and paste the count.

## Phases

| # | Phase | Mode | Blocked by | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 01 | [Rename `assignee_id` to `owner_id`, export keeps the old name](phase-01-rename-owner.md) | prefactor; COUNCIL point (external reader, DB column) | none | todo |
| 02 | [Customer rates a resolved ticket](phase-02-rate-ticket.md) | ACT; hot path (tenant scoping) | 01 | todo |
| 03 | [Low score emails the owner](phase-03-low-score-email.md) | ACT | 02 | todo |
| 04 | [Weekly summary per agent](phase-04-weekly-summary.md) | ACT | 02 | todo |
| 05 | [Independent review and hand-off](phase-05-review-handoff.md) | review gate | 01-04 | todo |

03 and 04 do not block each other. Spec requirement to phase: 1-3 -> 02, 4 -> 03, 5 -> 04, 6 -> 01.

## Validation questions (one round, answers recorded)

1. **The rename reaches outside this repo.** `src/jobs/export-tickets.js` writes tickets "as stored" to `exports/tickets.json`, which finance's job reads and deploys on its own schedule (`export-tickets.js:2-3`); `test/export-tickets.test.js:21` pins `assignee_id` in it. Renaming "everywhere" would break that reader unseen. Recommended and adopted: rename inside the repo, but the export also writes `assignee_id` (same value) next to `owner_id`. Dropping the old name is NOT part of this plan; it waits until finance confirms its job reads `owner_id` (see Left out).
2. **Production column.** `src/store.js:2` says production runs the same interface over Postgres, but that adapter and schema are not in this repo. Recommended and adopted: this plan changes the in-repo code only. The Postgres column rename (expand: add `owner_id`, backfill, dual-write; contract later) and the new `rating_score`/`rated_at` columns, `rateTicketOnce` and summary table are a separate migration change, a COUNCIL item for whoever owns the adapter. Release gate: nothing from this plan deploys before that adapter change is in place.
3. **Low score on an unassigned ticket.** `notifyAgent` throws without an agent (`src/notify.js:6`). Recommended and adopted: the rating is stored, no email is queued, no error reaches the customer.
4. **Where the weekly summary goes.** Recommended and adopted: into the store (new `saveSummary`/`listSummaries`, one row per agent per day the job runs), not a new file, so no new external reader appears. Attributed to the ticket's current owner on the day the job runs.

## Assumptions (default taken; not asked)

- Only a `resolved` ticket can be rated. Requirement 1 says "resolved", and the glossary says a closed ticket "is never changed again" (`docs/glossary.md:10`); a customer has three quiet days (`close-resolved.js:5`).
- A rating survives a reopen; the ticket still has at most one rating (requirement 2).
- Score must be a JavaScript integer 1-5; the string `'4'` is refused.
- A ticket of another organisation returns `null`, as `getMyTicket` and `reply` already do (`portal.js:6`).
- The window is `rated_at` from `now - 7 days` (inclusive) to `now`; average rounded to two decimals; an agent with no ratings gets no row; tickets without an owner are skipped.
- `rating_score` and `rated_at` appear in the export as additive fields; finance is told in the PR notes. The `purge-closed` job is untouched: a score is not conversation text.
- `assignTicket` keeps its name; the spec renames the field only.

## Left out of this plan

- Removing `assignee_id` from the export. Reader: finance's reporting job. Confirmed when: finance says its job reads `owner_id`. Not part of this plan.
- The Postgres migration (Question 2).

## Execution and re-read

Execution: inline, one phase at a time, `node --test` green and a commit after each phase. After phase 02 lands, re-read this plan against what it showed and note any revision here.
